00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:02.580
- [Instructor] So what we
have here on this number line

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.890
that we've now marked off with the tenths

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.210
and you can see that this
is three tenths here.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:11.720
We can think about this as a
multiplication of a decimal.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.890
And so what is this representing?

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:14.820
And I'll give you a hint.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.280
It's representing something
times three tenths.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.721
So pause the video and
try to think about that.

00:00:20.721 --> 00:00:21.568
Well, let's see.

00:00:21.568 --> 00:00:25.360
We are going one times three tenths,

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.130
two times three tenths,
three times three tenths,

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.550
and then four times three tenths.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:36.550
So what's represented here
is four times three tenths,

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:40.023
and so what is this going to be equal to?

00:00:40.023 --> 00:00:42.780
Well you can see you go from three tenths,

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.450
to six tenths, to nine tenths,

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.590
and then you could view
this as twelve tenths,

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:49.470
but twelve tenths is the same thing

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:52.230
as one, one and two tenths.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:55.250
So you could view this as 1.2.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.130
One and two tenths.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.840
Let's do another example.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.670
No, actually I'll do it
on the same number line.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.160
If we wanted to represent

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:09.160
three times 0.2

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.580
What would that look
like on this number line?

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.640
And what would this be equal to?

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.192
So I'll put a little equal sign here.

00:01:17.192 --> 00:01:20.100
Pause this video and see
if you an figure that out.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.470
All right, so let's think
about where two tenths is

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:25.230
this is one tenth, two
tenths is right over there.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:29.620
This is 0.2, and we're gonna
multiply it times three.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.059
So, we're gonna multiply it times one,

00:01:32.059 --> 00:01:34.444
then we're gonna multiply it times two,

00:01:34.444 --> 00:01:35.460
that takes us to four tenths

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.630
and then we're gonna
multiply it times three

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:41.243
to get us to six tenths, 0.6.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.890
So it's six tenths just like that.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.100
Now you could also visualize two tenths

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.810
as parts of a whole.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.100
So for example, this
represents two tenths.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.629
I have this whole, this square is a whole

00:01:53.629 --> 00:01:57.080
it's split into ten equal columns here

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.330
and we have two of them filled in.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.010
So this represents two tenths.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.020
So if you have three times two tenths,

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.150
Well this is one times two tenths,

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:06.000
this is two times two tenths,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.360
and this is three times two tenths.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.700
And so how many tenths do we now have?

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:15.660
Well we have one, two, three,
four, five, six tenths.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:19.050
Which is exactly what we
have here, six tenths.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.660
Let's do one more example,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.650
that gets a little bit more involved.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.510
So here we're told to multiply.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.270
It says you many use the models shown

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:27.380
to help find the product.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.850
And this is a screen
shot from the exercise

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:30.970
on Khan Academy.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:31.820
So pause this video

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.560
and see if you can
figure out what this is.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.110
All right, so they're saying 52 hundredths

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.999
times three, and they have 52 hundredths

00:02:40.999 --> 00:02:42.840
depicted right over here

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.910
and then they have it
depicted three times.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:47.500
So the total number of
hundredths depicted here

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.420
that is 52 hundredths times three,

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.010
because we have 52 hundredths here,

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:54.520
another 52 hundredths, and
then another 52 hundredths.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.925
So how many hundredths
is that going to be?

00:02:56.925 --> 00:03:01.570
Well, you could view
this as 52 times three

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:05.290
and that will give you the
number of hundredths we have.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:06.720
So let's think about this.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.950
So if we were to just say 52 times three,

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.130
well this is going to be two times three

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:15.950
is equal to six and then
five tens times three

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:18.850
is 15 tens, which is the same thing.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.960
We either just write it as 15 tens,

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.789
or that's 100 and five tens.

00:03:22.789 --> 00:03:25.830
But either way if I have 52 of something

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.010
and I multiply that by three,

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.010
I now have 156 of that something.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.990
And here the something is hundredths.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:36.990
So if I say 52 hundredths times three

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:41.069
that's going to be 156 hundredths.

00:03:41.069 --> 00:03:45.960
And how do we represent 156 hundredths.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.660
Well there is a couple
of ways to think about it

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.880
if this is the ones place,
this is the tenths place,

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:53.040
this is the hundredths place.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.890
Well we would write the
six there, the five there,

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.140
and the one there.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.250
So you could recognize this as hey look,

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.140
a hundred hundredths,
let me color code it,

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:05.708
a hundred hundredths is
the same thing as a whole

00:04:05.708 --> 00:04:10.680
and I'll circle that in
red, and fifty hundredths

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.340
is the same thing as five tenths,

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:15.650
and of course six
hundredths is the same thing

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.310
as six hundredths.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:20.753
So this is going to be equal to 1.56,

00:04:21.889 --> 00:04:24.190
or you could view this as 156 hundredths,

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:25.820
or you could view this as a whole,

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.310
which is a hundred
hundredths, and five tenths,

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:31.563
which is fifty hundredths,
and six hundredths.

